sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Model fidelity to source: 76/100" ;
        rdfs:comment "The script accurately implements the intra-hypercolumn Fourier harmonics (Eq. 3.12), anisotropic Fourier- Bessel lateral coupling weights (Eq. 4.9), second-order Rayleigh-Schrödinger dispersion curves lambda_even/odd(q), and the exact two-regime log-polar retino-cortical map with analytic inverse and tangent orientation map phi_R = phi + theta_R, matching all 5 stability_reports and all 24 preset runs in paper- calibration.json to 2.22e-16. However, amplitude_gamma2 and amplitude_gamma3 compute only unweighted local orientation overlap integrals without the spatial lateral-kernel weighting, quadratic-mode feedback, or quintic terms of Bressloff et al. (2001 §5, Eqs. 5.12-5.15), which prevents rolls and squares from ever stabilizing, leaves odd-branch H0/Hpi degenerate (eta_hex = 0), and causes 12 of 133 paper-expectation checks to fail (-10 pts). In stability_scan and branch_selection_for, presets with fixed parity != critical_branch (such as fig29_* and fig30_*) evaluate the even eigenfunction at the odd branch's critical_q and growth rate, and roll_stable checks 2*gamma_3(theta) > gamma_0 only at the preset's rendering angle pattern_angle_deg rather than across all theta (falsely reporting roll_stable=True in CSV rows 9, 10, and 12) (-5 pts). Furthermore, _eval_xy maximizes |a(r, phi)| rather than signed activity a(r, phi), introducing sign-flip jumps across nodal lines that double the contoured hexagonal spatial frequency (k* = 21 vs 11 cycles), and orientation_eigen_details truncates at m=4 with an ad-hoc +-1.5 clamp vs m=10 in branch_coupling_sum (-5 pts). Finally, the wavenumber scaling k = q*/d_hyp with upstream alpha, beta, and xi_hat_lat = 1.5 yields a cortical wavelength lambda_c = 8.68 mm (11 cycles) that is 3.1x longer than the paper's 2.4-3.2 mm (30-36 stripes), and the Rule et al. (2011) panel has no dynamical or Floquet solver (-4 pts). Evidence: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L519–L599: Fourier harmonics W_n, Fourier-Bessel lateral coupling W_n^lat(q), and O(beta^2) perturbative dispersion relation branch_growth <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L519-L599>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L672–L859: Unweighted orientation-overlap integrals amplitude_gamma2/amplitude_gamma3 and branch_selection_for where roll_stable only tests pattern_angle_deg <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L672-L859>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L946–L960: stability_scan evaluates branch_selection_for at critical_q of critical_branch even when eff_params.parity is fixed to the opposite branch, and sets wave_number = critical_q / hypercolumn_mm <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L946-L960>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L1069–L1093: _eval_xy selects argmax_phi |a(x, phi)| via np.abs(val) > np.abs(best), flipping signs across nodal boundaries <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L1069-L1093>." ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-model-fidelity> ;
        pk:hasProbability "0.76"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-model-fidelity> rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants (2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py, docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif, bressloff_v1_metrics.csv, datasets/bressloff/horton_hoyt_1991_magnification.json) satisfies the MorphoEval 0.1.0 criterion 'Model fidelity to source' for Homo sapiens primary visual cortex (V1) — geometric visual hallucinations (Klüver form constants) and flicker phosphenes" ;
        dct:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (Cursor agent, blinded second assessor)" .
}

sub:provenance {
    sub:assertion prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1001/archopht.1991.01080060080030>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00336965>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.2000.0769>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1137/23M1616686>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1162/089976602317250861>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1002158> .
    <https://doi.org/10.1001/archopht.1991.01080060080030> dct:date "1991"^^xsd:gYear ;
        dct:title "The representation of the visual field in human striate cortex: a revision of the classic Holmes map" .
    <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00336965> dct:date "1979"^^xsd:gYear ;
        dct:title "A mathematical theory of visual hallucination patterns" .
    <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.2000.0769> dct:date "2001"^^xsd:gYear ;
        dct:title "Geometric visual hallucinations, Euclidean symmetry and the functional architecture of striate cortex" .
    <https://doi.org/10.1137/23M1616686> dct:date "2024"^^xsd:gYear ;
        dct:title "A mathematical model of the visual MacKay effect" .
    <https://doi.org/10.1162/089976602317250861> dct:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
        dct:title "What geometric visual hallucinations tell us about the visual cortex" .
    <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1002158> dct:date "2011"^^xsd:gYear ;
        dct:title "A model for the origin and properties of flicker-induced geometric phosphenes" .
}

